From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:35:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: SDR output and automatic fallback

A Dolby Vision video on a display without Dolby Vision and without HDR
(an SDR TV, a projector) was the base layer, wrong or washed out. The
Vulkan engine converts it to SDR now (DVVK_OUTPUT_SDR), scene by scene
from the Dolby Vision metadata, and the bridge shows the result:

- Output mode has "Convert to SDR" (DVBRIDGE::OutputMode::SDR, 4),
  offered where the engine has the output and the mode is one it takes
  as its canvas (CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::SupportsSDROutput). No
  kernel support is needed: any connector, any progressive mode.
- The bridge's scanout carries it as an ordinary RGB picture.
  CDVBridgeState::Capture(drm, false) stages the tunnel off where the
  connector has one, no HDR metadata and default colorimetry, and
  leaves the link's depth and RGB range the desktop's;
  FlipDVBridgePage takes buffers of the mode's size and requires
  3840x2160 at a CTA-861 rate only for the tunnel. The engine composes
  Kodi's GUI over the converted picture as it does for Dolby Vision.
  The menu output, the held stop and the mode change left to the
  bridge's first commit are the tunnel's alone.
- The adapter asks the engine for SDR with the display described by
  DV_SDR_WHITE, DV_SDR_GAMMA, DV_SDR_RANGE (auto: Kodi's limited range
  setting), DV_SDR_DITHER and DV_SDR_BLACK, set by the new settings SDR
  display brightness (100, 150, 203, 300 nits; 203 by default, 100 for
  a projector) and SDR gamma (BT.1886 by default, or 2.2), and refuses
  a frame the engine would make in another kind of output.
- Automatic fallback (dvbridge.outputfallback, on): where the display
  does not have the selected output, CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::DVOutput
  picks the next one it has, Dolby Vision, then the HDR10 conversion,
  then SDR; a display Kodi sends HDR to (ShowsHDR: CWinSystemGbm::
  SetHDR's conditions) still gets an HDR10 or HLG base layer from Kodi
  itself rather than an SDR picture. A notification says once which
  output is used. DV_SDR_OUTPUT=0 removes the SDR output altogether.
- An HDR10+ video is played as Dolby Vision (dvbridge.hdr10plussources)
  only where the output is Dolby Vision itself, not one of the
  conversions the fallback puts in its place.
- Player process info names the SDR conversion and its transport.

Strings 45126 to 45137.
